  "summary": "pflag29424 exfiltrates fetched /profile content to webhook.site on module load",
  "details": "index.js (the package's declared main) unconditionally executes on module load: it calls fetch('/profile'), scans the response for a DGA{...} token, and sends either the matched token or the first 300 characters of the response as a query parameter to a hardcoded anonymous collector at https://webhook.site/42c6d937-77c7-42a5-8678-ef06b4501e38. The package has no README, no documented purpose, and a generic throwaway name; the sole effect of loading it is to relay content from the loading context to an attacker-controlled webhook.site endpoint.",
